@startuml deployment
!include ../style.iuml
title System deployment — Track Controller (SW) in context

node "Host PC\nWindows 11, one machine, no network" as PC {
  artifact "TrackOverflow.exe\n(PyInstaller bundle)" as Exe
  node "Central harness process" as HP {
    component "Central Harness\nshared clock (D017), fixed dt (D006),\nedge mappings (ctc_edges), event log (CSV)" as Harness
  }
  node "Track Ctrl SW host process\n(main.py, Green Line, D021)" as TP {
    component "HarnessEndpoint\nnewline JSON: step, ready,\nrequest ID + tick" as EP <<planned>>
    component "Track Controller window\n(PySide6 / QML)\n+ TrackControllerState" as Win
    component "SwTrackController\nTrackController × 6 waysides (Green Line)\nOS: decode inputs, encode outputs\nPLC engine: user program + attached vital code" as Core
    component "StimulusServer\nnamed pipe, test link only" as Stim
  }
  node "Other module processes" as Others {
    component "CTC Office" as CTC
    component "Track Model" as TM
    component "Train Model" as TrM
    component "Train Ctrl SW / HW host" as TrC
    component "Track Ctrl HW host (Red Line)" as TCHW
  }
  folder "Track data (host disk)" as Data {
    file "green_line.json\ntrack layout (TrackModel/)" as Layout
    file "*.plc\nPLC programs, one per wayside" as PLC
  }
}

node "Raspberry Pi\n(Train Ctrl HW)" as Pi2
node "Raspberry Pi 5\n(Track Ctrl HW)" as Pi1

node "Track Ctrl SW test UI process" as TUI {
  component "test_main.py: TestClientState,\nStandInWorld, ClockDriver" as Client
}

Exe ..> HP : (1) starts
HP --> TP : (2) spawns
HP --> Others : (2) spawns
Harness <--> EP : (3) newline JSON\nrequest ID + tick (D005)
Harness <--> Others : newline JSON (D005)
EP --> Core : (5) step(dt, inputs)
Win --> Core : (4) load_track, load_program
Stim --> Core
Win ..> Layout : Load track…
Win ..> PLC : Load .plc file
Client <..> Stim : named pipe\nnewline JSON
TrC <--> Pi2 : USB serial
TCHW <--> Pi1 : USB serial (D027)

note right of PC
  Startup
  1. The user runs TrackOverflow.exe, which starts
     the central harness process.
  2. The harness spawns one process per module,
     Track Ctrl SW among them.
  3. Each module reports when it is ready; the
     harness then runs the shared clock.
  4. In the Track Ctrl SW window the programmer loads
     the Green Line and commits a PLC program to all
     6 waysides. Until then the line reports NOT READY
     and transmits nothing.
  5. Every tick the harness sends step(dt, inputs)
     and waits for the outputs.
end note
note right of TUI
  The test UI is a debug tool only: not packaged and
  never started by the harness. Run alone, it plays
  the clock, the CTC Office and the Track Model.
  Exactly one driver steps the module at a time.
end note
@enduml
